<h2 id="reaserch-groups">Reaserch groups</h2>

<ul>
  <li>
    <p><a href="https://gsf.institutlouisbachelier.org">GSF</a>: Reaserch group in the field of green and sustainable finance, hosted by ILB.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><a href="https://www.fime-lab.org">FDD Fime</a>: Research group in mathematical finance/economics applied to the energy sector.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p><a href="https://impt.math.cnrs.fr">IMPT</a> (France) and the <a href="https://www.imperial.ac.uk/mathematics-planet-earth">MPE</a> (England) are research groups  that develop mathematical modelling tools for studying Planet Earth, its life-supporting capacity, and the impact of human activities.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.stockholmresilience.org">Stockholm Resilience center</a> is a research center working on the concept of resilience i.e. “the capacity of a system, be it an individual, a forest, a city or an economy, to deal with change and continue to develop”. The seminal publication about planetary boundaries can be found <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/461472a">here</a>.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.ngfs.net/en/liste-chronologique/ngfs-publications">NGFS</a> is a research group which aim at strengthening the global response required to meet the goals of the Paris agreement and to enhance the role of the financial system to manage risks and to mobilize capital for green and low-carbon investments in the broader context of environmentally sustainable development.</p>
  </li>
</ul>

